-- title:
--   Degree of a level quotient for Ogg's unit on X₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $j(q^d)$ for the divisors $d$ of $p$. Write $u =$ `modularUnitSeries p` for the Laurent series $\Delta(q)\,\Delta(q^p)^{-1}$, where $\Delta$ is given by $q$ times the power series unit attached to the Dedekind eta function, and assume $u \in F$. Let `Afin p` be the subalgebra `chartAlg ℤ F {jFull p}` of $F$ furnished by the two-chart integral model construction over $\mathbb{Z}$ for the single element $j \in F$ (the finite chart), and let $v \in$ `Afin p` be an element whose image in $F$ is either $u$ or $p^{12} u^{-1}$. Let $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ be monic with $g(0) \neq 0$. Then the $\mathbb{Q}$-vector space
--   $$\bigl(\mathbb{Q} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} \mathrm{Afin}\,p\bigr) \big/ \bigl(1 \otimes g(v)\bigr),$$
--   the quotient by the ideal generated by the single element $1 \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} g(v)$ (with $g(v)$ evaluated in `Afin p`), has finite $\mathbb{Q}$-rank equal to $(p-1)\deg g$, the equality being one of natural numbers.
--
--   The element $u = \Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ is Ogg's modular unit on $X_0(p)$, of degree $p-1$ with polar divisor supported on the cusps; the statement computes the degree of the affine zero divisor of $g(u)$ on the cuspidal complement, the hypothesis $g(0) \neq 0$ keeping the zeros away from the cusps. It feeds the computation of stalkwise ranks in [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.rankAtStalk_levelRing_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.rankAtStalk_levelRing_eq).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_HpoolLevelRing_finrank_rat_tensorProduct_quotient_span_aeval.lean

